@startuml
hide footbox
skinparam defaultFontName Microsoft YaHei
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
title S04-structured-sequence — source snapshot (not a runtime trace)
participant "obj: 调用者" as obj
participant "gw: GatewayController" as gw
participant "route: RouteRegistry" as route
participant "boundary: AuthBoundary" as boundary
participant "http: IdentityClient" as http
participant "ctl: AuthController" as ctl
participant "auth: AuthorizationService" as auth
participant "proxy: ProxyClient" as proxy
activate obj
obj -> gw: 1. forward(request)
activate gw
gw -> route: 2. resolve(request.method, request.URI)
activate route
deactivate route
gw -> boundary: 3. authorize(operationId, bearer)
activate boundary
boundary -> http: 4. check(operationId, bearer)
activate http
http -> ctl: 5. api(actor, operationId)
activate ctl
note over ctl
Identity verified first; DDD unknown aud becomes 401 TOKEN_INVALID, not 404.
end note
ctl -> auth: 6. api(userId, systemCode, operationId)
activate auth
deactivate auth
deactivate ctl
deactivate http
alt invalid identity / unknown operation / denied / timeout
boundary --> obj: GatewayFailure 401 / 403 / 503
else allowed
note over boundary
Only HTTP 200 with matching operationId and non-null allowed is interpretable.
end note
deactivate boundary
gw -> proxy: 7. forward(request, bytes, traceId)
activate proxy
deactivate proxy
note over proxy
Course object-level 403 is preserved.
Gateway does NOT invent course success audit or course Service methods.
end note
end
deactivate gw
deactivate obj
@enduml